Enhancement: Warn about PHP versions with known critical vulnerabilities

The security & setup warnings in the admin settings now report a PHP version
that lacks the fixes for the critical vulnerabilities of the PHP interpreter
published on 21 October 2026 (CVE-2026-109618 and CVE-2026-109619, remote code
execution without authentication). They are fixed in PHP 8.2.35, 8.3.36,
8.4.27, 8.5.12 and 8.6.0RC4; older branches get no fix and are pointed to the
supported 8.4 branch.

The warning is an error for upstream builds. For distribution builds (a PHP
version with a distribution suffix, for example from Ubuntu) it is only a
warning, because distributions often ship the fix with an older version
number. Once the fix is installed that way, 'php_security_check' => false in
config.php hides it.
